  "body": "What is missing: PR #1086 adds the MCP tool `edit_tool` (edit a tool through the same undoable command the GUI uses), but the camcraft-mcp skill (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/`) has no row for it, and the PR names no follow-up. Found in the review of PR #1086 (issuecomment-6841183170).\n\nWhy: AGENTS.md \"Commands ship with an MCP tool\" - the agent surface keeps up with what shipped; owed skill rows are P5.\n\nScope: add the `edit_tool` row (parameters, DTO shape, undo behaviour, refusals) to the skill's tool table. It can ride with #1337 (the `set_operation_coolant` row) in one PR. A skill change is a process change: bump `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` and announce it on #681.\n\nDone means: the camcraft-mcp skill lists `edit_tool` with its parameters as shipped, and `PROCESS_VERSION` is bumped.\n",
